0,Ata language - WikipediaYele – West New Britain languages - WikipediaWest New Britain Music Association- WNBMA - FacebookListen to New Britain radio stations online - best New ...,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ata_language,"The Ata language, also known as Pele-Ata after its two dialects, or Wasi, is a Papuan language spoken on New Britain island, Papua New Guinea. It appears to be related to neighboring Anêm, and possibly also to Yélî Dnye in a proposed Yele-West New Britain family. Yele – West New Britain is a tentative language family proposal by Malcolm Ross that unites three languages: Anêm and Ata (Wasi) of western New Britain, and more dubiously Yélî Dnye (Yele) of Rossel Island. The Ancient Dusk ""Village Boy"" music program is gaining momentum. We are finalizing Ward 4 with the reemergence of our village's iconic StringBand, the ""Creek-Siders StringBand"" of Bola Village. Listen to your favorite New Britain, United States music for free without registering at Onlineradiobox.com.",Pele-Ata,Yele-West New Britain
