5,"Ata language - Alchetron, The Free Social Encyclopedia",https://alchetron.com/Ata-language,"Apr 25, 2026 · The Ata language, also known as Pele-Ata after its two dialects, or Wasi, is a language isolate spoken on New Britain island, Papua New Guinea. It may be related to the Anêm and Yélî Dnye isolates in a tentative Yele-West New Britain family.",Pele-Ata,Yele-West New Britain
